BASIC 
PRINCIPLES OF 
OOP (OBJECT￾ORIENTED 
PROGRAMMING)
▪ Class - A class is a template or blueprint from which objects are created. 
It describes a set of objects with the same behaviour. A class can contain 
Fields, methods, constructors, blocks, nested class and interface. To create 
a class, you use the keyword class.
public class Major {
Int x = 10;
}
▪ Object - An object is an instance of a class. It is an entity that has state 
and behaviour. It can be physical or logical (tangible and intangible).
public class Main {
int x = 5;
public static void main(String[] args) {
Main myObj = new Main();
System.out.println(myObj.x);
}
}
▪ Abstraction - The process of hiding the details and exposing only the 
essential features of a particular concept or object without including the 
background details or explanation.

